        "id": 139269,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-11T11:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My partner and I got together through gaming. Well, it started off just <span class=\"bbcode-i\">talking</span> about gaming, where we'd chat about Minecraft and the Yogscast at work. Well, we'd <span class=\"bbcode-i\">try</span> to, but then we'd actually have to do work and stuff so would never be able to finish a conversation. So I got bored of that and just gave him my e-mail address as he'd mentioned having Skype, so he added me on there and we were able to chat properly. He's dyslexic and types really slowly so we started using voice chat, and I can remember messing around in a single-player game of Minecraft while we discussed various games that could be played online. I mentioned Titan Quest (an ARPG like the Diablo games but with an ancient mythlological setting) and was talking about how fun it was and stuff and he ended up getting it so we played that together, and went onto other games but I think we'd actually \"got together\" by that point. Sentinels is just one of many games we've played together, and these days tend to get in at least a couple of games when he's round my house most weekends. Outside of that we chat on Skype every evening (except the ones where we're at one of our houses, of course ;)) and play whatever online game it is we have on the go atm…which currently is Diablo III, replaying it together now the expansion is out and stuff. I would call this run-through fun but disappointing as we've only been going a couple of weeks but we're max level already, finished Campaign Mode the other day, and neither of us have died once :P.</p>",
