        "id": 139271,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-11T15:47:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I find myself surpressing my love for tabletop around my girlfriend. She knows it's a hobby of mine, but she is just not into it unless it's Cards Against Humanity and there is a good beer near by. She told me once that one of her last Ex forced her to play this awful boardgame <em>constantly</em> and she hated every second of it (she didn't remember which game though). It really put her off on anything tabletop which makes it that much harder to even suggest we try a game together. You kinda have to play around the \"you're just like my Ex\" card, so to speak.</p><p>I have my tuesday night gaming group though and shes wonderful about never seeing me on those nights.&nbsp;</p>",
